{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554033-going-into-hiding","id":1554033,"title":"Going into hiding","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-09-27T10:44:39-07:00","id":1554033,"title":"Going into hiding","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">So</span> a thought experiment, let's say a mage needs to go <span style=\"font-size:14px\">into</span> hiding; they banged the heirarch's daughter, stole the local tetrarch's most valuable comic book whatever. <br /> <br /> What <span style=\"font-size:14px\">arcanums</span> would be the most helpful here?<br /> <br /> Space seems like an obvious one, using it to either conceal or destroy any sympathetic connections the mage might have to prevent them from being found or tracked, along with being able to just teleport to somewhere very far away.<br /> <br /> Are there any other arcanums/tricks that would be useful?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26144-eshangray","name":"eshangray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-27T11:18:44-07:00","id":1554034,"title":"","content":"Death and Prime to mess with physical and magical forensics, plus Time to cut off pre- and postcognitive investigations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-27T18:08:06-07:00","id":1554036,"title":"","content":"Veiling is a Practice common to all Arcana, so sufficient creative use of that in combination with mundane technique to do so should give any mage at least a fighting chance.<br /> <br /> I think Dave Brookshaw's original Actual Play that put him on the map and the path to becoming the game's developer for a while was cognizant on the point that the greatest defence a mage can have is not having consistent enough routines that enemies even know where to point their all-seeing eye in the first place. Something like Postcognition is powerful sure, but... a mage still needs to know where and when to look, and have yantras for sympathy to those targets. You can hardly just summon up the entire history of a subject at will and peruse it at leisure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-28T14:26:31-07:00","id":1554038,"title":"","content":"Anything that helps you survive on your own in your hiding place is also welcome. <b>Life</b>, <b>Matter</b> and <b>Forces</b> come to mind. The less you have to go out and/or interact with anything to forage for resources, the less you risk leaving evidence behind. <b>Mind</b> may help you deal with witnesses without making them into more evidence.<br /> <br /> But the corollary for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a>'s first point is that every Arcana can be used to track you, and not necessarily through direct evidence. Knowing which Arcana or mundane skills the people going after you have is also important and can substantially change what are your best approaches to hide. <b>Space</b>, <b>Death</b> and <b>Prime</b> are good all-purpose tools, but depending on the specifics of who's following you and how they may barely do anything.<br /> <br /> Your best starting point is <b>Death</b> and <b>Prime</b>, anyway, so you can get rid of evidence, together with mundane skill. While <b>Space</b> and <b>Time</b> may be second due to their particular effectiveness at gathering general information, even those two in the end are conditional on whatever your stalker has at hand. Messing with as much basic information as possible is the only relatively reliable method to delay someone from picking on your tracks.<br /> <br /> Other than that... move around? Hiding for extended lengths of time is more a matter of staying ahead of whomever is looking for you than hoping to stay hidden forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-29T09:59:21-07:00","id":1554048,"title":"","content":"Each Arcana has a lot to offer in regards to hiding, but the 4 I would recommend are:<br /> <br /> <b>Death: </b>Pass through walls by going into Twilight, hide as a shadow, erase your Nimbus, avoid leaving forensic evidence, hide your presence entirely and even fake your death.<br /> <br /> <b>Life: </b>Allows you to live in and adapt to any environment, covers healing, you can move around without worrying about nourishment, you can disguise yourself completely and even hide as an animal.<br /> <br /> <b>Prime: </b>Probably the best at hiding from Supernal tracking, not great if your pursuer can call in favors with other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> <b>Space: </b>Makes you difficult to track sympathetically, allows you to see around corners, cross obstacles, teleport away, create resting locations whose access points are difficult to find, creates a pocket space, allows you to carry everything you need on you and can create protective barriers.<br /> <br /> Strategically speaking, your best bet is to draw your pursuer's attention away. Mages are incredible investigators and their powers are very flexible, a mage with enough time and determination will find a way. But if the mage has higher priorities, or if their are layers of misdirection regarding who caused the issue, then those act as a buffer for your safety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 09-29-2025, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-30T05:36:39-07:00","id":1554054,"title":"","content":"Okay, I had misremembered exactly what the book said about how Active Mage Sight interacts with concealment powers.<br /> <br /> In the course of trying to look back for confirmation or denial of it, I find I honestly have no clue how to read what it's saying about when Active Sight can and cannot see through such concealment.<br /> <br /> Like, for its examples... why is Mind Sight affected by invisibility but Life Sight is not? Like, shouldn't Mind be able to detect a consciousness for the exact same reason that Life can perceive a living presence?<br /> <br /> And like, it's saying that concealment only works if it would logically mask from the purview of the Arcanum, but doesn't work if the concealment and Sight &quot;use the same principles&quot;? And a psychic-based stealth power is given as an example of something that won't work against Mind, so what the fuck does &quot;logically mask from the purview&quot; actually mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-30T08:57:56-07:00","id":1554058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554033-going-into-hiding?p=1554054#post1554054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I had misremembered exactly what the book said about how Active Mage Sight interacts with concealment powers.<br /> <br /> In the course of trying to look back for confirmation or denial of it, I find I honestly have no clue how to read what it's saying about when Active Sight can and cannot see through such concealment.<br /> <br /> Like, for its examples... why is Mind Sight affected by invisibility but Life Sight is not? Like, shouldn't Mind be able to detect a consciousness for the exact same reason that Life can perceive a living presence?<br /> <br /> And like, it's saying that concealment only works if it would logically mask from the purview of the Arcanum, but doesn't work if the concealment and Sight &quot;use the same principles&quot;? And a psychic-based stealth power is given as an example of something that won't work against Mind, so what the fuck does &quot;logically mask from the purview&quot; actually mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading of that section has generally been that Mage Sight in general requires you to be able to perceive the thing you're pointing your Sight at, much as with the clarification of Peripheral Mage Sight in Signs of Sorcery.<br /> <br /> Mind Sight lets you tell if something you're looking at is a thinking being, but without Attainments, Merits, or other modifiers to the way your Mage Sight works, it's not going to let you see the invisible if that invisibility doesn't have anything to do with messing with the Mind. Meanwhile, Life Sight deals with living things, for which sensory camouflage is a relatively common trick \u2014 if the Life Arcanum doesn't let you spot a chameleon, it's not exactly doing its job.<br /> <br /> It's a known poor example, but it has some sense to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-30T13:43:53-07:00","id":1554061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554033-going-into-hiding?p=1554058#post1554058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, Life Sight deals with living things, for which sensory camouflage is a relatively common trick \u2014 if the Life Arcanum doesn't let you spot a chameleon, it's not exactly doing its job.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it hard to accept that as a resolution when the text talks in terms of photons.<br /> <br /> (Obligatory pedantry that chameleon colour changing has more significance for social signalling and temperature regulation than camouflage)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 09-30-2025, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-30T14:40:44-07:00","id":1554064,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the example is the result of the wording of the two sights being a bit different. Mind sight &quot;detects the presence of thinking beings&quot;, whilst Life Sight &quot;detects life signs&quot;. So to me Mind sight sounds like it just tells if a thinking being is present, not where they are, whilst Life sight would inform you of life signs that aren't impacted by the invisibility (I dunno, heartbeat? Respiration?).<br /> <br /> To be honest, I don't really buy this, but you never know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-30T16:28:22-07:00","id":1554065,"title":"","content":"I think the easiest way to avoid any potential way of tracking you is to stop being you.<br /> <br /> Like if you die then symbolically you are a dead end.<br /> <br /> In Time you have a Lacuna, in Space yeah, sure you might now have a ghost left behind, but is that really you or just a collection of memories that the pissed off party might still decide to track down?<br /> <br /> Fate will probably not be able to track you is what I'm saying, cause you is not.<br /> <br /> Of course there may be other, less permanent ways to not be you. Join the Blank Badges legacy? Maybe. Still pretty permanent change. But it is very Occultation driven.<br /> <br /> Going somewhere that is not worth the effort of following may also help (like the Hedge/Underworld/an Emanation realm) of course what you can survive while your pursuer(s) can't depends on relevant circumstances, skills and arcana... But what I'm saying is, there is more than just Arcana to think about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-30T17:03:50-07:00","id":1554067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554033-going-into-hiding?p=1554061#post1554061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it hard to accept that as a resolution when the text talks in terms of photons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. I said &quot;sensory&quot; instead of &quot;visual&quot; for precisely this reason, but you're welcome to come up your own explanation for the example or make your peace with it being a bad example one page distant from a sidebar explaining the subjective calls needed for Mage Sight in relation to other supernatural beings. The Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle gives multiple examples of what different Mage Sights can glean of different parts of changeling miens through the Mask, and the corebook is explicit that Active Mage Sight only provides its information within the scope of the character's senses. Active Mage Sight alone is not See Invisibility.<br /> <br /> The two examples are highlighting different parts of concealing powers' interaction with Active Mage Sight: On the one hand, a supernatural power that doesn't interfere with the Arcanum's purviews doesn't stop it from working \u2014 an unambiguous example is that a spell to make you impossible to see through remote-viewing magic does not block a mage from looking at you with Life Sight in person even if it would prevent them from doing so through a scrying window \u2014 and on the other hand, a supernatural power that works on the same principles as an observing mage's Active Sight can be Clashed with by that Sight \u2014 the same spell could be pierced by Space Sight, assuming it works on magical principles involving Space.<br /> <br /> More examples in the same vein:<br /> <br /> The Deviant Variation Camouflage, which makes the character invisible (and, at higher Magnitudes, scentless and undetectable by sound), does not allow a mage to spot its user with Spirit Sight (assuming the Variation does not stem from a spiritual origin), because its effects concern physical invisibility rather than simply making thinking beings ignore their existence like Obfuscate, but Forces Sight can pierce the concealment because the Variation is messing with light (and possibly sound) in a way that that Arcanum can potentially detect.<br /> <br /> The Dread Power Gauntlet Cloak, which makes the character functionally invisible by displacing its user just parallel to the material world, meanwhile, would not register to Forces Sight (the character is not so much distorting light and sound as it is simply not present in the phase of reality being looked at), but would register to Spirit Sight (because the power works by distorting the Gauntlet).<br /> <br /> A spell to make a sleeping person appear dead does not interact with Time Sight, Space Sight, or Forces Sight (assuming it is not transposing information from another time or place or projecting a light/sound/thermal/pressure-based illusion), but naturally intersects with the principles of Life, Death, and Mind Sight, because being able to tell if a body is alive or dead or asleep is a specific type of information those Sights can provide.<br /> <br /> The basic principle is sound, it's just the one example of piercing visual invisibility with Life Sight but not Mind Sight that is less than airtight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-01T08:05:38-07:00","id":1554081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554033-going-into-hiding?p=1554067#post1554067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. I said &quot;sensory&quot; instead of &quot;visual&quot; for precisely this reason, but you're welcome to come up your own explanation for the example or make your peace with it being a bad example</div> </div> </div> </div>See, the example annoys me a lot less than the fact that I find the base description of how it works to be confusing, and the example only adds to that.<br /> <br /> Like, it seems to be saying that concealment works both if it does and doesn't interact with the Arcanum of an Active Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> Just, what does &quot;logically mask from purview of the Arcanum&quot; mean? What does &quot;concealment using the same principles of the Arcanum&quot; mean? How can both of these things be true at once?<br /> <br /> If you use Forces to become invisible, is that something that logically masks from Forces, or is that something that is using the same principles as Forces that allows one to see through it?<br /> <br /> It strikes me as such an unnecessarily convoluted approach when it would have been so easy to just have something like &quot;Mage Sight doesn't render concealment a lot less useful by being able to intrinsically see that there is concealment there (even if you can't see what's underneath it), but it does let you lose Clash of Wills to potentially see concealment&quot;.<br /> <br /> Have I used Forces to turn invisible? Then you're invisible without conflict to most Arcana. Can Forces Mage Sight let you see that Forces is being used to create invisibility? Only if you win on Clash of Wills. Can Prime be used to tell that a spell is hanging in the air there? Also only with Clash of Wills. Simple.<br /> <br /> The thing that annoys me is that we have this whole process for providing resolution for how conflicting powers works built into the foundations, and then this section not only disregards it but does so by introducing terminology otherwise not relevant to the magic system. I'd be a lot less thrown off if &quot;uses the same principles&quot; showed up anywhere else in the text.<br /> <br /> Part of how it throws me is that I find it introduces a weird doubt to how the Veiling Practice interacts with the Knowing and Unveiling Practices. Like, if Mind Mage Sight is the one that will see through a psychic form of concealment, why does a Veiling of Mind work on any other Mind spell intended to find out exactly the sort of information that the Veiling would be intended to stop? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-01T15:46:14-07:00","id":1554088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554033-going-into-hiding?p=1554081#post1554081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, the example annoys me a lot less than the fact that I find the base description of how it works to be confusing, and the example only adds to that.<br /> <br /> Like, it seems to be saying that concealment works both if it does and doesn't interact with the Arcanum of an Active Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> Just, what does &quot;logically mask from purview of the Arcanum&quot; mean? What does &quot;concealment using the same principles of the Arcanum&quot; mean? How can both of these things be true at once?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, does the whole rundown I gave in the rest of my post not help clarify this?<br /> <br /> The &quot;logically masking&quot; part is because not every type of concealment magic applies to all senses \u2014 Shield of Chronos isn't going to do anything to stop people from looking at you outside the context of looking at your past or future, Death Sight isn't going to help you detect that an object has been made to seem more valuable than it is, etc.<br /> <br /> The &quot;concealment using the same principles&quot; part is because not every supernatural concealment method is a straightforward use of the Arcana, but a supernatural effect that conceals something using methods that fall under the purview of an Arcanum can be detected by Mage Sight of that Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Using Forces to become invisible logically masks the subject from the purview of Forces, because objectively not being able to be seen masks a subject from the purviews of most Mage Sights attached to a person with eyes that need the base phenomenon to reflect in the visible spectrum to attach Symbols to it; <i>at the same time</i>, Forces Sight in particular has a chance to pierce the invisibility because the invisibility is happening as a function of messing with Forces \u2014 you would not get that opportunity with Time Sight or Space Sight, because the concealment does not use Temporal or Spatial principles, and because the thing it's concealing is the visible presence of the subject there isn't a whole angle of approach that those Sights can see like how Suppress Life doesn't prevent Spirit Sight or Matter Sight from perceiving the subject's supposedly-dead body.<br /> <br /> Invisibility powers are a unique wrinkle in explaining this, because the stipulation exists purely to clarify that if a spell conceals one thing but not another then Mage Sights that don't deal with the thing being concealed don't have a chance to get anything out of it, and for invisibility powers the thing being concealed is &quot;the presence of a subject that can be observed.&quot;<br /> <br /> Knowing and Unveiling spells are spells, and in those cases where a Veiling Spell does not provide a Withstand rating to be overcome with Potency the observational spells Clash with the Veil as normal but with the benefits available to a spell (i.e. Advanced Duration and Potency). Mage Sight can be used in a pinch, but depending on your Path and Legacy an appropriate spell as a Rote or Praxis can bypass the Mana surcharge that would otherwise come with using a non-Ruling Arcanum (or the Willpower cost of sustaining the Sight for extended periods of time, or the penalty to actions unrelated to using or perceiving magic). It's delineating a fallback option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-02T06:54:22-07:00","id":1554101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554033-going-into-hiding?p=1554088#post1554088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using Forces to become invisible logically masks the subject from the purview of Forces, because objectively not being able to be seen masks a subject from the purviews of most Mage Sights attached to a person with eyes that need the base phenomenon to reflect in the visible spectrum to attach Symbols to it; <i>at the same time</i>, Forces Sight in particular has a chance to pierce the invisibility because the invisibility is happening as a function of messing with Forces \u2014 you would not get that opportunity with Time Sight or Space Sight, because the concealment does not use Temporal or Spatial principles, and because the thing it's concealing is the visible presence of the subject there isn't a whole angle of approach that those Sights can see like how Suppress Life doesn't prevent Spirit Sight or Matter Sight from perceiving the subject's supposedly-dead body.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that's a consistent way to reconcile the stated elements, although I'd still be pissed off that the book would use such a circuitous way to express it. And the examples given leave me with a lingering question about whether or not to just dismiss them as bad examples* or if they mean reading the interaction like this in the first place is still not the intended result.<br /> <br /> Although frankly, I still think it's kind of annoying to have an interaction based on a premise that the method for hiding from a particular avenue of scrutiny is also the kind of thing that actually gives it away.<br /> <br /> * And not even bad as in &quot;confuse more than they clarify&quot;; more like &quot;outright contradict the preceding statements&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}